  "servings": 3,
  "summary": "Discover the vibrant taste of South American street food with this innovative Brazilian flatbread that brings rich cassava flavors straight to your table. Prepared entirely within <b>a single cast-iron skillet</b>, this one-pot method eliminates extra cleanup while building rich toasted aromas directly into the tender tapioca dough. The skillet first browns seasoned ground pork and diced bell peppers, capturing every bit of savory flavor before the hydrated cassava starch is dusted into the warm pan to form a crisp, molten cheese-stuffed crust. Fresh cilantro and shredded canastra cheese add bright herbal notes and a creamy melt that binds the hearty filling together seamlessly. Cooking everything sequentially in one skillet ensures that no seasoned pan drippings are wasted during the baking phase. Ideal for quick weeknight dinners or cozy weekend gatherings, this flatbread offers a delightfully chewy texture alongside a golden crispy exterior that will impress family and friends alike.",
